      "f1000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001": {
        "tag": "rich-text",
        "id": "f1000001-0000-7000-8000-000000000001",
        "content": "# Focal Denoising as Left Kan Extension (Riehl)\n\nThe ncreel layout algorithm is a left Kan extension:\n\n```\nLan_focus(F|_focused) = Render\n```\n\n\"The rendered layout is the best approximation of the full reel state given that we start from the focused tablet.\"\n\nThis is exactly what the man page describes:\n> A redraw starts with the focused tablet... its callback is invoked with a plane as large as the reel... Tablets are successively lain out in these spaces until the reel is filled.\n\n## Categorical Structure\n- F: Cylinder -> Tree -> Syrup (the abstract reel state functor)\n- focus: {focused} -> Cylinder (inclusion of the focused tablet)\n- Render: Cylinder -> Plane (the layout rendering)\n- Lan_focus(F|_focused) = Render (the universal property)\n\nThe focused tablet gets the entire reel if it needs it (maximum capability). Remaining tablets share what's left (attenuated capability). This IS the Kan extension: the best extension of partial data to the full domain."
      },
